**Known for**: JeffGeerling YouTube channel, blogger

Jeff hosts a reasonably successful YouTube channel where he often posts videos
about FOSS, open hardware, and Linux, and a blog with supplementary materials.

Jeff is a Catholic anti-abortion and anti-contraception advocate, and has
written several blog posts on the subject between 2011 and 2013.[[source]][0]
Popular YouTube channel Practical Engineering aimed to collaborate with him in
2025, but retracted his support after the community pointed out Jeff's
politics.[[source]][1] Jeff was informed of the reason why Practical
Engineering did not wish to collaborate with him, but has not issued any
apologies or retractions for his earlier statements.

Jeff did delete two blog posts following the call-out, one where he re-iterated
his anti-abortion position in the cases of rape and incest,[[source]][2] and
another where he argued that a "genetic disposition to homosexuality" was not
"okay".[[source]][3]

